title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf duplicate trash
catalog: CLI command
target: mf duplicate trash
summary: Trash the copies a query matches, where a twin exists outside it

!! Reference

```
Trash the copies a query matches, where a twin exists outside it

In every group with a copy outside the query, the copies matching it go to the trash; a group wholly inside the query is left alone, so no group loses its last copy. Lists the copies and asks first.

Usage: mf duplicate trash [OPTIONS] <QUERY>

Arguments:
  <QUERY>
          DSL query selecting the copies to trash (e.g. `mfr_path ->* "/old"`)

Options:
  -s, --simplified
          Treat the query as simplified-language text and expand it first

      --dry-run
          List the copies that would be trashed, and stop

  -y, --yes
          Skip the confirmation prompt

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
